:"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T17:32:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T17:32:45Z","body":"> > Just noticing this right now, but we have the same issue with `end_line` and partially `end_column` as well, no? It just doesn't cause this specific crash.\r\n> \r\n> Ah I think you're right! Should be a good fit for this PR. I can do some testing and an update in the morning (currently late PDT here).\r\n\r\nUpdated PR with some `end_line` and `end_column` sanitation. I could not find a crash with them. `make_token` sets them to sane values most of the time.\r\n\r\nI did find some edge cases in surrogate pairs. `end_line` and `end_column` were pointing a bit farther than the leading surrogate about which the error message complained. I cleaned those up (the `prev_line` / `prev_column` cases) and improved the tests to check both start and end positions. You can see the new test cases in my recent force push above.\r\n\r\n```\r\n[doctest] test cases:  1 |  1 passed | 0 failed | 1403 skipped\r\n[doctest] assertions: 72 | 72 passed | 0 failed |\r\n[doctest] Status: SUCCESS!\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5037091769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_g